cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MINERVA, please cite the paper below (preferred citation) and this software."
title: "MINERVA: MInimum observations for accurate Exoplanetary mass estimation with Radial Velocity Analysis"
type: software
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/EXOPA-OAPa/MINERVA"
authors:
  - family-names: "Di Maio"
    given-names: "Claudia"
    email: "claudia.dimaio@inaf.it"
    affiliation: "INAF – Osservatorio Astronomico di Palermo, Italy"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   # <- insert your ORCID and uncomment
keywords:
  - radial velocities
  - exoplanets
  - planetary masses
  - stellar activity
  - observation planning
  - Monte Carlo simulations
  - Ariel
abstract: >-
  MINERVA estimates the number of radial-velocity (RV) observations required to
  measure the masses of transiting planets orbiting FGKM-type stars to a given
  precision. It simulates realistic RV time series on real observational
  timestamps, models stellar activity from age, rotation and chromospheric
  activity through empirical calibrations, and recovers the planetary signal
  with an incremental periodogram and least-squares fitting procedure.
